<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70704" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηπῐ-έη</span></b> , ἡ, 
			Ep.
		 form for *<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηπιίη</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήπιος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>childhood, childishness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴνου ἀποβλύζων ἐν νηπιέῃ ἀλεγεινῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.491
				</span></i>
			: in pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ τί σε χρὴ
			νηπιάας</span> (for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νηπιίας</span>) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀχέειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.297
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὶ . . ποιήσῃ ἀθύρματα νηπιέῃσιν</span>”
				<i>in childish fashion,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.363
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡγήσατο νηπιέῃσι</span> led
			them <i>in his folly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.469
			</span></i>.</div>
